    "count": 5,
    "label": "Restricted Electives",
    "notes": "Five upper-division and/or graduate-level courses from PHYS 100–195 and 200–295 (twenty units). Students may use a maximum of two courses outside of physics to satisfy this requirement, provided they come from a single focus area and are listed (Astrophysics: ECE 120, MAE 180, ASTR 123, 150; Biophysics: BI** 100–185, CHEM 100–186, not BISP courses, BIEB 176, CHEM 130; Computational physics: MATH 170A-B-C, 179, 183; Materials physics: CHEM 120A-B, ECE 103, 134, 135A-B, 136L, MAE 160; Physics of the Earth, Oceans, and Atmosphere: SIO 103, 111, 171, 172, 177). All courses applying to the restricted electives must grant four or more units. CHEM 130 is not accepted (CHEM 100–186 is written as 100–129 and 131–186)."
   }
